---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pricing" description="Chudware is entering commercial preview. Explore browser, native desktop, and organization access while public pricing is finalized.">
  <header class="page-hero pricing-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial preview</p>
      <h1>Pricing, without placeholder numbers.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Public rates and packaging are being finalized for launch. Rather than publish invented figures, this page shows the ways Chudware can be used and sends you to the right next step.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap access-grid">
      <article class="access-option access-primary">
        <p class="eyebrow">Browser workspace</p>
        <h2>Open Chudware from a tab.</h2>
        <p>Each browser seat runs in an isolated rootless container and streams the application as video. There is no desktop installation to manage.</p>
        <ul class="fact-list"><li>Full parametric modeling workspace</li><li>Assemblies, CAM, PLM, simulation, and reverse engineering</li><li>AI copilot inside the product</li></ul>
        <a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a>
      </article>
      <article class="access-option">
        <p class="eyebrow">Native desktop</p>
        <h2>Run on your workstation.</h2>
        <p>Native Chudware preview builds exist for Windows and Linux and are currently available on request rather than through a public release channel.</p>
        <ul class="fact-list"><li>Windows and Linux preview builds</li><li>OCCT 7.9 geometry kernel</li><li>Access coordinated on request</li></ul>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">Native access details</a>
      </article>
      <article class="access-option access-contact">
        <p class="eyebrow">Organizations</p>
        <h2>Planning for multiple seats?</h2>
        <p>Talk directly with Chudware about access, deployment, and support requirements while the commercial catalog is being finalized.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com">Contact sales <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pricing-principles">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What is settled</p>
        <h2>The product modes are real. The public rate card is not ready.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The browser service, isolated seat architecture, and native desktop application exist today. Exact rates, storage allowances, credit bundles, discounts, and tier boundaries will appear only after they are ratified.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="pricing-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this page changed</p>
        <p>The previous pricing table used layout filler. Publishing a clean-looking guess would be less useful than being explicit about commercial-preview status.</p>
        <p>Account creation and sales contact remain available while the final catalog is prepared.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choose a route</p>
      <h2>Start in the browser or inspect the native build.</h2>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">View downloads</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
